// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - DocAeon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P2739687221" "Capture Dr. Aeon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2243410667" "Dr. Aeon keeps ranting about 'the old fool'..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2290739586" "You have captured and interrogated Dr. Aeon."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2986634840" "You're not gonna believe this, but Daos himself questioned Aeon, and then let him go! Doctor Aeon's alibi is rock-solid, and Daos says he didn't have anything to do with it. The portal's still offline 'till they understand what went wrong last time, but maybe that'll work, too. Sound like you got some leads from Aeon to look up."
// RandomFameString :
"P2194272438" "Poor Dr. Aeon. What does {VillainName} have against that guy?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1998247569" "I tracked down some info on that 'Diviner Maros' guy Aeon was talking about. Did you know him? He's this weird Circle of Thorns guy out on Sharkhead. I never liked those wizards, and ever since I found out the truth about them, the whole ancient-ghosts thing, I mean, I like them even less. Anyway, the weird thing with him is even most of the rest of the Circle stays away from him, so he works with villains instead. It might be a trap, but if what Dr. Aeon says is right, your best lead is to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>talk to Diviner Maros.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2334348742" "Talk to Diviner Maros."
// SendOffString :
"P4034291800" "So this Maros character is supposed to be able to tell you where to go to learn about what Professor Echo told Dr. Aeon? This is making my head spin! Get it sorted out so we can carry on with Operation: Destiny. <br><br>We didn't attack Peregrine Island and then fight off the Nemesis Army just to give me a migraine, after all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2603683957" "Talk to Diviner Maros"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2470038954" "Just try to get a straight answer out of this Diviner Maros guy. <br><br>Man, I hate ghosts."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2814569473" "How many times have we met? How many times have I talked to you, oh 'Destined One'? It's hard to keep track, now. No, you're working with Black Scorpion, so you're part was holding off the Army of Brass, not stealing the gate to the Beyond, or capturing the great minds. And have we worked together before? I cannot separate out the history you know from all the sea of what might have been. But I know this moment. You were sent to me by Professor Echo, who told his younger self to send you to me, just as he remembered. That's the problem with time travel. The sense of a story can get confused when the events happen in a different order. <br><br>Fourteen thousand years ago, we called it The Tower, but really it was a portal. We of Oranbega sought to build a gateway to the heavens to re-awaken our gods in our time of need, we could not have foreseen that it would come to this. When it failed, my mind was opened to every possible moment between then and the future you're racing towards. Soon, you will enter the portal and decide fate itself. Lord Recluse has learned of this. He's left his notes nearby, in this chain of events. I'll only learn that you found them too late, of course, and I won't be able to stop you. Not that I want to, I am eager to see a world where I don't know what's going to happen, and would hate to see you destroy it in a war with Arachnos. <br><br>Now where did I later learn you found those notes? Ah, yes. I remember that when I learned about it, I was surprised it was on this very island. It would be ironic if I didn't already know what's going to happen. I'll show you where I later learned you went."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2305198893" "Investigate Base"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1262279528" "No, don't tell me what he said. I looked up an entry on him in the database and I'm already confused. Just check out the base he told you about. From what I can tell, it's one of ours, but so secret not even Mako knows it's there, and he's supposed to be running that Island. Hah! What a drip!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P3610158318" "This is the place Maros showed you. But what could be here?"

