// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - AeonsLastEcho 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P1483065196" "Find Dr. Aeon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1880078577" "Dr. Aeon dropped a notebook before he disappeared."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P965633132" "You've learned what you needed to learn in the future."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P81269761" "The future dies because of all of this? Because of Operation: DESTINY? I knew this plan was a bad idea! But that makes a strange kind of sense. I learned what was in those journals. Lord Recluse knew that what you saw was a possible outcome of all this. Some of the Fortunatas can see into the future and stuff, and they told him. Reading his journal, Recluse figured there were only three ways it's gonna go: Either he gets the future he wants but the world dies, like you saw; or he gets what he wants but then you die before you can become a threat; or his destiny might never get fulfilled. Guess which one he wants to make come true?"
// RandomFameString :
"P2828892090" "It felt like {VillainName} was walking over my grave. Spooky."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3686266122" "Let me make sure I understand this: The Dr. Aeon from the destroyed world like 15 years in the future thinks you need to beat Lord Recluse in the near future so you can show the Recluse in the present that it's too risky to fight you over control of Arachnos, which would happen if he uses you in Operation: DESTINY unless he double-crosses you and kills you before that happens. No, I still don't get it. But I do get that you gotta show Recluse who he's messin' with, and you need to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>get the Destiny Portal altered to do it.</A>"
// AcceptString :
"P2404050631" "Get Destiny Portal altered."
// SendOffString :
"P204609887" "I was thinking about it, and my first plan was for you to kidnap researchers while disguised as Manticore. Then I realized that since you're the 'Destined One', you could probably just ask people, and they'd do it for you. To make it even easier, I copied Recluse's signature out of one of his journals and put it on some paperwork for you. I figure you should probably talk to Grant Naylor first, he's this geek they have out on Nerva who knows a lot about portal stuff. But to get any of it done, you'll have to talk to Operative Grillo."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission5_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2065507677" "Talk to Naylor in Nerva"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1789822718" "Grant used to work for me, you know? Back when he was just a soldier. I knew it was a good idea to keep Mantis from killing him because of his accent."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2455806461" "Good ta' see ya, {VillainName}. Now that Operation: DESTINY's in full swing, nobody's tha' interested in me work no more. An' there's so much ta learn. I think the Circle might have tried some really crazy experiments with these portals years and years back. Might have tried to reach the other side, if ya know what I mean. Anyway, what's on yer mind? <br><br>Re-adjust the DESTINY Portal? I been tellin' Grillo that he needs ta test that thing more, but just because I don't 'ave his fancy degrees, he never wants ta listen to me.  Well, I can write up how ta do it for ya, sure."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission5_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1745053173" "Take papers to Grillo"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P461143460" "Grillo's been really useful to me over the years, with all the armor improvements I've made. I'm glad you won't have to rough him up."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P509765257" "Ah, Destined One, the portal isn't ready for the next test, but it will be soon. What's this? <br><br>Re-alignment test? The idea does have merit, even if it is from Naylor. Well, you do have all the authorization, and that is Lord Recluse's signature. Very well, I'll have the next test altered. It should give us some important data, at least."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P815381325" "You take some forged paperwork."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1529401596" "They bought it? Great! Now all that's left is gonna be Recluse himself."
// RandomFameString :
"P2381991589" "Something big is about to happen, and {VillainName} is sure to be in the center of it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1321872609" "This is it. Look, I've been helping you out because I hate to see somebody get screwed like that. I mean, yeah, we fought and you won, and I'm still angry about that, but the way Recluse has messed with you, that's too much. And he's been playing with everyone's future, too. But to <A HREF={ACCEPT}>travel into the future to attack and defeat Lord Recluse</A> to show him who's boss? That's just crazy. You'll really need to have a gang with you, or it's suicide. Maybe even then!"
// AcceptString :
"P1137738067" "Travel to the future and battle Lord Recluse"
// SendOffString :
"P1334305382" "I get it, I get it. There's no talking you out of this. Well, it's all ready and set up. If you still have any friends, I'd say call 'em in. And no, I won't help you on this. I may not be happy with what Lord Recluse has been planning, but I won't double-cross him for this. <br><br>But hey, {VillainName}? <br><br>Good luck."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission6_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3228285661" "Defeat Recluse in the Future"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2923132635" "The Destiny Portal is already set up. All you have to do is go through it, fight past the Arachnos troops who'll probably have shoot-on-sight orders for you, and then defeat Lord Recluse himself."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1641442712" "This is it. If you defeat Lord Recluse here, at his moment of triumph, you can break the cycle of doom. Recluse may have sought you out as one of his Destined Ones, but this moment is your Operation: Destiny."
// ExitStringSuccess :
